 "text": "Hi, how have you been? That's normal. It' the bearings wearing in, getting quieter. It won't last, and you' hear it for years to come. You could, but it' stick the chain to the roof of the chain ring during stops. Much easier to fix a loud chain than a stuck one. Pour it over the chain, not in the jump between the rollers, and wipe off the excess. A thin film sticks anyway. Clean it, yes. A dry chain makes more noise anyway. Not really. A few minutes of lubing every few hundred miles is enough.",
